            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Telugu for a lemon, then the Telugu for grapes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: జామపండు",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "జామపండు — jāmapaṇḍu — \"a guava\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "జామపండు (jāmapaṇḍu) is jāma, usually traced to Sanskrit jambū, \"the rose-apple tree\" (CDIAL 5131), a name passed on to the guava, and native paṇḍu, \"fruit\" (DEDR 4004), which DEDR compares with Sanskrit phala."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
